ed","id":"20075914"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"21765418"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"9882445"}],"value":"Heterohexadecamer of 8 large chains and 8 small chains (PubMed:9882445, PubMed:17574029, PubMed:7922027); disulfide-linked (PubMed:8245022). The disulfide link is formed within the large subunit homodimers (Probable) (PubMed:17574029, PubMed:7922027, PubMed:8245022). The exposed C-terminus binds in a cleft in the RbcX2 (shown with endogenous and Anabaena strain CA protein) (PubMed:20075914, PubMed:21765418). RbcX2 is displaced by RbcS; as RbcX2 is removed RbcS mediates the ordering of an internal RbcL loop (Thr-64-Leu-70) in a catalytically active conformation (Probable) (PubMed:17574029, PubMed:21765418)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P00880","intActId":"EBI-9023246"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"A0A0H3K9R3","geneName":"rbcX","intActId":"EBI-15936812"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P00880","intActId":"EBI-9023246"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q44212","geneName":"rbcX","intActId":"EBI-9023244"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":true}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q31NB3"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"In the carboxysome RuBisCO is organized into a paracrystalline array (By similarity). This cyanobacterium makes beta-type carboxysomes (Probable)"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_01338"}],"value":"Carboxysome","id":"SL-0034"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21765418"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"20075914"}],"value":"Binding of RbcS probably induces a conformation change that displaces RbcX2 and triggers the final mature conformation"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"8245022"}],"value":"The disulfide bond which can form in the large chain dimeric partners within the hexadecamer appears to be associated with oxidative stress and protein turnover"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17574029"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21765418"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"20075914"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"21765418"}],"value":"RuBisCO folding and assembly commences when the nascent large subunit folds with the help of the chaperonin GroEL-GroES. Monomers require chaperone RbcX2 to assemble into RbcL8 octamers yielding RbcL8-(RbcX2)8 (Probable) (PubMed:17574029). RbcX2 is displaced by RbcS; as RbcX2 is removed RbcS mediates the ordering of an internal RbcL loop (Thr-64-Leu-70) in a catalytically active conformation (Probable) (PubMed:17574029, PubMed:21765418)"}],"commentType":"MISCELLANEOUS"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8245022"}],"value":"The basic functional RuBisCO is composed of a large chain homodimer in a 'head-to-tail' conformation. In form I RuBisCO this homodimer is arranged in a barrel-like tetramer with the small subunits forming a tetrameric 'cap' on each end of the 'barrel'"}],"commentType":"MISCELLANEOUS"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the RuBisCO large chain family. Type I subfamily"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":472,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Ribulose bisphosphate carboxylase large chain","featureId":"PRO_0000062651"},{"type":"Motif","location":{"start":{"value":461,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":467,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"descrip